put(G[5]+'/README.md','# Downstream utility attribution\n\n**Purpose:** inspect whether cosine relevance is a useful proxy for the reader’s context-specific unit utility. This is post-freeze VAL diagnosis, not fresh confirmation or universal causal necessity.\n\n**Inputs:** saved source units, original predictions, exact deletion interventions and source/group identities. **Output:** unit importance = original task score minus score after deletion; positive/exact-zero/negative categories follow the preserved sign rule. QA uses answer F1; SciFact inference uses its registered correctness/label behavior, not per-example macro-F1.\n\n**Open first:** '+link('src/week12_attribution/experiment.py',doc=G[5]+'/README.md')+'. Core functions are perturb, prepare and execute.\n\n**Main results:** '+link(unit,doc=G[5]+'/README.md')+'; **relevance statistics:** '+link(corr,doc=G[5]+'/README.md')+'. See the local equation/code map and J/K/L notebooks.\n\n**Finding:** many units are neutral and many associations weak/uncertain, with condition-specific positive exceptions. Neutral deletion does not prove unused evidence, and a harmful deletion effect is conditional on the rest of the context. Original perturbation output shards are missing; preserved tables cannot substitute for those receipts. Do not claim all semantic relevance failed.')
put(G[9]+'/README.md','# Final matched method comparison\n\n**One canonical home** for FIXED_SENTENCE, QBGF_FULL, BEA_QBGF_V1, post-hoc BEA_V2 and MINILM_CE_SENTENCE on the shared50queries/dataset at256/1024. This is exploratory developmental data, not the full W12 VAL surface or reserved confirmation.\n\n1. '+link(matched,doc=G[9]+'/README.md')+' — recorded formatted point estimates.\n2. '+link(eff,doc=G[9]+'/README.md')+' — recorded quality/cost summaries.\n3. '+link(pairs,doc=G[9]+'/README.md')+' — saved paired intervals, raw p-values and24-comparison Holm family.\n4. '+link('W12-POST/results/minilm_reranker/analysis/POINT_ESTIMATE_WINS.json',doc=G[9]+'/README.md')+' — descriptive only.\n\n**Code:** comparison_table/analyze in '+link('W12-POST/reranker_baseline/analysis.py',doc=G[9]+'/README.md')+'. **Notebook:** '+link(G[9]+'/notebooks/1_final_baseline_comparison.ipynb',doc=G[9]+'/README.md')+' (same canonical MiniLM notebook, not an independently generated comparison).\n\nHotpot’s strongest point estimates are post-hoc V2; QASPER FIXED/QBGF; SciFact MiniLM. No MiniLM contrast survives its registered Holm family. No universal winner or retrospective replacement of the frozen method follows. See docs/final_interpretation.md and the case-study evidence ledgers.')
put(G[9]+'/docs/final_interpretation.md','# Interpretation\n\nPoint estimates are task-dependent. MiniLM is highly competitive on SciFact, FIXED/QBGF are close in QASPER, and static reranking does not reproduce the strongest post-hoc V2 Hotpot estimates. These are previously analyzed development cohorts, small and exploratory. No MiniLM comparison passes its saved24-family Holm correction. Original W12 final policy remains FIXED_SENTENCE; no exploratory result revises it.\n\n'+link(matched,doc=G[9]+'/docs/final_interpretation.md')+'; '+link(pairs,doc=G[9]+'/docs/final_interpretation.md')+'.')
