put('DATASET_AND_EXPERIMENT_SETUP.md','# Dataset and experiment setup\n\n| Dataset | Project task / candidate evidence | Primary metric | Frozen W12 VAL | Reserved confirmation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| QASPER | Scientific-paper QA; complete matching paper is the retrieval corpus | Answer F1; EM secondary where recorded |1005queries/281paper groups |0; historical TEST already consumed |\n| HotpotQA | Multi-hop QA; provided distractor context paragraphs, not a newly retrieved whole-Wikipedia corpus | Answer F1; EM secondary |7155queries/7155groups |200queries/200groups |\n| SciFact | Claim verification over all provided corpus abstracts, never just the cited/gold document | Three-class macro-F1; accuracy/per-class and invalid-format diagnostics |177claims/157groups |50claims/43groups |\n\nThe corpora and tasks stress different forms of evidence use: multi-source combination, scientific-paper context and label-sensitive claim verification. Those are task descriptions, not proof that one allocator universally solves them. SciFact invalid outputs count under the original parser; no parser repair based on results occurred.\n\nCommon W12 pipeline: query → pinned SFR-Embedding-Mistral → candidate pool capped at10 → exact source units/allocator →256or1024serialized evidence tokens → Qwen/Qwen3-8B BASE_FP16 with no LoRA. Query/instructions/chat framing are outside the evidence-token allowance; output caps are separate. The exact source-block token IDs are inserted into the prompt. Short original pools are preserved, not padded.\n\nQA generation cap128; verification cap16; max context8192; greedy do_sample=False; seed42; Qwen thinking disabled in chat construction, as frozen configuration/source specifies. These reader parameters are not evidence budgets. Confirm against '+link('configs/week12/protocol.yaml')+' and '+link('src/week12/reader.py')+'.\n\nW11 is a smaller exploratory50-query-per-dataset pilot with its own action grids/retrieval width and reader controls; it must not be described as identical to W12. Historical W2–W7 use earlier SARA surfaces/checkpoints.\n\nV1 pilot, LOO, V2 post-hoc and MiniLM share50developmental queries/dataset. V1 expansion has150/dataset and includes the pilot. These are not fresh confirmation. QASPER is paper-grouped, SciFact uses cited-document components, Hotpot normalized-question groups; frozen TRAIN/VAL/CONFIRM are group/ID disjoint.\n\nExact membership/source identity: '+link('results/week12/qbgf/v3/protocol/W12_SPLIT_FREEZE.json')+'; '+link('results/week12/qbgf/v3/protocol/split_summary.json')+'. Missing historical raw outputs and external weight/data dependencies remain listed in UNRESOLVED_PROVENANCE.md.')
# High-level entry points retain nuanced scientific status and unresolved evidence limits.
put('README.md','# Query-Conditioned Budget-Aware Evidence Allocation for Retrieval-Augmented Generation\n\n**Defense working folder: FINAL_PROJECT_MAIN/**. All changes in this pass are confined here. No algorithm logic or notebook cells were changed and no experiments ran.\n\n**Start with:** [ALGORITHM_DEFENSE_GUIDE.md](ALGORITHM_DEFENSE_GUIDE.md), [CODE_MAP.md](CODE_MAP.md), [NOTEBOOK_MAP.md](NOTEBOOK_MAP.md), [RESULTS_INDEX.md](RESULTS_INDEX.md), and [IMPORTANT_NUMBERS.md](IMPORTANT_NUMBERS.md). Dataset/metric details: [DATASET_AND_EXPERIMENT_SETUP.md](DATASET_AND_EXPERIMENT_SETUP.md).\n\nThe research story is quantity → identity → granularity → relevance → downstream utility. Final frozen W12 policy: **SFR top10 → FIXED_SENTENCE → Qwen3-8B BASE_FP16**, evidence budgets256/1024, no LoRA. QBGF was not promoted universally. BEA/MiniLM are later exploratory work; V2 calibration failed and its tau8e-5 reader branch is post-hoc.\n\n'+ '\n'.join(str(i+1)+'. ['+g.split('_',1)[1].replace('_',' ')+']('+g+'/README.md)' for i,g in enumerate(G))+'\n\nEach method has local numbered code views, configs, untouched notebooks, results and docs where applicable. Code views are internal symlinks to exact canonical modules; no artificial module split or duplicate algorithm implementation was created. Raw/query-level results are retained when available. Top-level src/scripts/results aliases serve compatibility, not primary navigation.\n\nScientific-status/chronology/cohort documents distinguish validation, freeze, confirmation, post-freeze attribution and post-hoc exploration. The [provenance manifest](PROVENANCE_MANIFEST.csv) records exact source identities and every curated rename.\n\n**Readiness limit:** missing original W12 full validation/confirmation raw shards and attribution perturbation receipts still prevent full independent historical verification. [UNRESOLVED_PROVENANCE.md](UNRESOLVED_PROVENANCE.md) states this explicitly. This pass improves defense navigation; it does not manufacture missing evidence or turn archived notebooks into safe run launchers. Many saved flags already enable full generation/install work; do not Run All for a viva. See DEFENSE_READINESS_REPORT.md.')
