put('COHORT_MAP.md','# Cohort map\n\nSee DATASET_AND_EXPERIMENT_SETUP.md for exact W12 counts and grouping. The frozen split is '+link('results/week12/qbgf/v3/protocol/W12_SPLIT_FREEZE.json')+'.\n\n- W12 VAL: Hotpot7155, QASPER1005, SciFact177.\n- Reserved confirmation: Hotpot200/200groups, SciFact50/43groups, QASPER0.\n- LOO/V1 pilot/V2/MiniLM: same50queries/dataset from VAL; four-method post-hoc1200rows plus MiniLM300rows.\n- V1 expansion:150queries/dataset, includes pilot, still VAL.\n- Qualitative cases: retrospective subset, not prevalence estimates.\n\nOriginal TRAIN/VAL/CONFIRM IDs and group assignments were not regenerated. Full VAL, confirmation and matched pilot cannot be treated as paired cohorts.')
put('REPRODUCIBILITY_MAP.md','# Reproducibility and entry-point map\n\nFor each central method CODE_MAP.md identifies main code, runner, config, notebook, primary and statistical results. NOTEBOOK_MAP.md adds inputs, outputs and unchanged switch values. Local README files explain the inspected algorithm and actual historical entry interface.\n\nThis archive has exact recorded result bytes and method code, not a fully installed portable research environment. External datasets and pinned weights/SARA checkpoints, original package/code identities and missing historical raw W12 output shards are still needed for independent reproduction. Current source snapshots are not assumed identical to historical freeze commits.\n\nNo benchmark, training, retrieval, predictor fitting, calibration or generation was rerun. Original V2 calibration remains terminated. The separate post-hoc notebook does not repair that status. Archived model/install/full-run switches may already be True; opening code and tables is the intended viva workflow.\n\nMetadata-only verification (from the repository root) is available after this pass:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 FINAL_PROJECT_MAIN/11_shared_infrastructure/audit/verify_defense_archive.py\n```\n\nThis verifies copies, source hashes, navigation and notebook preservation; it does not reproduce experimental science.')
put('DEPENDENCY_AUDIT.md','# Dependencies and preserved implementation\n\nCanonical original package layout is retained under11_shared_infrastructure/runtime. Numbered local code files are internal symlinks to those modules; they are navigation views, not executable standalone rewrites. Relative import context matters when executing a viewed module directly; use its original entry script in a restored environment.\n\nInternal original-relative config/result aliases were rewired to the new canonical result locations. Notebook cells, absolute dataset paths, source-version guards, model/parser/prompt definitions and package pins were preserved. No refactor, formula, threshold, tie-breaking or serializer change was made.\n\nRemaining limitations: native corpora/weights/checkpoints are external; historical W12 C/D/M raw outputs and attribution perturbations are missing; the demo dependency list is not a complete research lock; old namespace packages named src require correct original launch context. Static syntax/link checks do not establish all dynamic third-party imports or model execution.\n\nHistorical migration/verification scripts are archived underaudit/previous_pass and12_report_support/previous_navigation; do not run obsolete paths after reorganizing. Use the new verifier only for metadata. Historical report links may still embed original paths; use the source map/provenance and current navigation. None of these issues was hidden by a new score or silently changed source artifact.')
put('UNRESOLVED_PROVENANCE.md','# Remaining provenance limits\n\n**NO — not yet fully independent as the sole evidence base for all four final-report/presentation/code/results-defense goals.** The navigation is defense-ready, but historical raw evidence gaps remain.\n\nOriginal full W12 C/D validation rows, reserved-confirmation answer rows and attribution perturbation/generation outputs are empty at their original locations. Aggregated tables, registered contrasts, historical reconstruction/closeout receipts and confirmation checksum inventory survive. They support reporting recorded results with this limitation; they do not permit independent current rescoring. Genuine backups are required, not invented/re-run replacements.\n\nV1 pilot/expanded raw rows and exact matched source pools, existing V2/control rows and MiniLM score/selection/answer rows are retained here when available. External native datasets, model weights/checkpoints and a complete historical environment are not bundled.\n\nOld curation prose misstated the final Qwen reader and V2 predictor type; it is superseded. Historical prose is not blanket-certified. Case-study automatic failure labels remain hypotheses absent human review; the report must not claim universal relevance failure, confirmed V2, statistical MiniLM superiority or fresh QASPER confirmation.\n\nNo method ownership ambiguity was resolved by inventing modules: local code views identify the same canonical real implementations. Exact source hashes, old/new paths and restored artifacts are recorded in the provenance and defense audit logs.')
put(G[10]+'/README.md','# Shared infrastructure\n\n`runtime/` is the canonical byte-exact source package layout. Method-local numbered code files point here. Reader/token-ID serialization, retrieval, sentence segmentation, task evaluation and storage are shared by reference, not copied into divergent algorithms.\n\n`data/matched_source_pools/` contains exact frozen source records for the developmental matched cohort. `audit/` contains source/path/symbol/notebook indexes, snapshots and metadata checks. Old pass scripts are retained historically; only the current verifier is intended after this migration.\n\nSee CODE_MAP.md, REPRODUCIBILITY_MAP.md and DEPENDENCY_AUDIT.md for launch/environment boundaries.')
put(G[11]+'/README.md','# Report support\n\n`source_reports/` preserves byte-exact historical reports, glossary and reconstruction/provenance material. `previous_navigation/` preserves superseded generated guides for traceability; their old paths and assertions are not current instructions.\n\nUse top-level IMPORTANT_NUMBERS.md and RESULTS_INDEX.md for numbers; ALGORITHM_DEFENSE_GUIDE.md/CODE_MAP.md for implementation explanations; SCIENTIFIC_STATUS.md and COHORT_MAP.md for claim boundaries. Do not let old prose override machine tables or fill missing historical evidence.')
